model surf07
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-30
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-03-31
  note "SURF-07: a day key where a date is expected means start_of(k) (LANGUAGE 3.1, tally 2.1). The same figure is asked both ways, max(opens, k) and max(opens, start_of(k)), over an index of days."

source fund_notice "The fund's notice: subscriptions open on 10 March 2026 (made up)"

index ds = day 2026-03-09..2026-03-11

input opens: date

def first_day[k in ds]: date = max(opens, k)

ask q_both: max(opens, k), max(opens, start_of(k)) for k in ds

ask q_def: first_day[k] for k in ds

version notice
  cite fund_notice
  governs always
  known 2026-03-01
  opens = 2026-03-10 "the notice"
